note    Frozen BEFORE any S3 scientific value (M_nd, omega1, omega2, gap, gray, mid,
        volume, density field, bound fraction) was read.  Section 16 discloses exactly
        what was already visible -- including that S3's M_nd and omega1 already exist
        in move_ladder_necessity/METRICS.json as rungs[3].Mnd_to / omega1_to, which
        were not opened before freezing, and that the per-rung cost figures were
        already known (which is why section 12 declines to invent a cost threshold).
        The materiality thresholds (S9), the production-relative acceptance gates
        (S10) and the relative-change denominator convention are inherited VERBATIM
        from earlier frozen preregistrations.  The objective bar remains 0.10 %.
